# Code owners are requested for review automatically on every PR.
#
# SETUP REQUIRED: replace @keduka-ai/maintainers with a real GitHub team or
# user handle. GitHub silently ignores CODEOWNERS entries that name a team
# which doesn't exist or lacks write access to the repo, so an unedited
# placeholder means no reviews are ever requested.
#
# For the rule to have teeth, also enable branch protection on `main` with
# "Require review from Code Owners".

* @keduka-ai/maintainers

# The security-sensitive surface. These files decide whether the container runs
# as root, what it can reach, and what gets executed on a user's machine —
# changes here deserve a deliberate look even when the diff is one line.
/Dockerfile                @keduka-ai/maintainers
/docker-compose.yml        @keduka-ai/maintainers
/docker-compose.cpu.yml    @keduka-ai/maintainers
/scripts/entrypoint.sh     @keduka-ai/maintainers
/install.sh                @keduka-ai/maintainers
/SECURITY.md               @keduka-ai/maintainers
/.github/workflows/        @keduka-ai/maintainers

# Dependency pins encode CVE floors and resolver ceilings — see
# CLAUDE.md § Dependency edits before approving a bump.
/requirements.txt          @keduka-ai/maintainers
/requirements-*.txt        @keduka-ai/maintainers
/jupyter-base.txt          @keduka-ai/maintainers
/pyproject.toml            @keduka-ai/maintainers
